<name>Japan 50 · While you're here (picks by day) + bench</name>
<description><![CDATA[Yellow stars: nothing scheduled, just the good options near where you already are that day. Import as a second layer on the same My Map and turn it on when you have a gap.]]></description>
<Style id="pick"><IconStyle><color>ff00d7ff</color><scale>1.0</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/ylw-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style>
<Style id="bench"><IconStyle><color>ff8ab7ff</color><scale>0.9</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/orange-stars.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><scale>0.8</scale></LabelStyle></Style>
<Folder><name>01 Tokyo · while you're here</name>
<Placemark><name>☆ Omoide Yokocho</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Nov 28</b><br/>Yakitori under the train tracks, 5 min from the hotel. If you want more than ramen.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Omoide+Yokocho&query_place_id=ChIJP9eKBdeMGGAR0zzBXJNVj5A'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.699578,35.692704,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Ramen Mitaba (Kabukicho, till 5:45am)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Nov 28</b><br/>Ramen 5 min from the hotel, open till 5:45am. The jet-lag bowl.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ramen+Mitaba+(Kabukicho,+till+5:45am)&query_place_id=ChIJ466CzkaNGGARpwPGpF4dx9w'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.703914,35.694468,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Imo Pippi (sweet-potato dessert)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Asakusa: crème-brûlée sweet potato, cash only, 11am open (so only if you&#x27;re still in Asakusa).<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Imo+Pippi+(sweet-potato+dessert)&query_place_id=ChIJ24IzFrqPGGAR3ptfNiVp9xo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.794411,35.714081,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Iyoshi Cola Asakusa Rokku</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Asakusa: craft cola made in front of you. Opens 12:30, so a Nov 30 Kappabashi add-on instead.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Iyoshi+Cola+Asakusa+Rokku&query_place_id=ChIJCdYEmyOPGGARIBZriyhh-Bo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.792583,35.712497,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Koffee Mameya</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Omotesando: the best coffee shop in Tokyo, no sign, beans from 20 roasters. 10–6.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Koffee+Mameya&query_place_id=ChIJB1oleKOMGGAR_10GNeoySkY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.710888,35.668368,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ The Roastery by Nozy Coffee (Cat St)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Cat Street: roastery + espresso martinis. On the walk between Micasadeco and Watchnian.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Roastery+by+Nozy+Coffee+(Cat+St)&query_place_id=ChIJCS0wmqaMGGAR2h4xKb_ah8c'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.704766,35.665572,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Sedai Coffee &amp; Roasters</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Harajuku: tiny roaster, 4.8, cheap. Two min from Micasadeco.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sedai+Coffee+&amp;+Roasters&query_place_id=ChIJ1aRTMACNGGAR8W16w3Uzd00'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.703052,35.664297,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ The Matcha Tokyo Omotesando</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Omotesando: matcha latte with a window over the street. 11–6:50.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Matcha+Tokyo+Omotesando&query_place_id=ChIJ17f1w_qNGGARfQzEoh19PyE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.706362,35.666928,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Menchirashi (carbonara udon)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Harajuku: the carbonara udon. 30-min line, next door to Micasadeco. Only if you skip Onodera.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Menchirashi+(carbonara+udon)&query_place_id=ChIJ651p-W-NGGARi41d0DEi2l8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.705091,35.666499,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Harry Harajuku Terrace (otter cafe)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Harajuku: the otter café. Reserve. Novelty, skip unless Mom wants the otters.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Harry+Harajuku+Terrace+(otter+cafe)&query_place_id=ChIJA0y7o6OMGGAROgRqIXDRAss'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.708007,35.669191,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Mega Don Quijote Shibuya</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Shibuya: 7 floors of Don Quijote, 24 hrs, tax-free on 7F. Souvenir run any night.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mega+Don+Quijote+Shibuya&query_place_id=ChIJr4J6pKmMGGARdQLOgrzToH4'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.697817,35.660387,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ The SG Club (Shibuya)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29</b><br/>Shibuya: one of the world&#x27;s top-50 cocktail bars, opens 6. Not on a jet-lag night.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+SG+Club+(Shibuya)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.699231,35.664243,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Iyoshi Cola Asakusa Rokku</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Asakusa: craft cola, 12:30–6:30, a 5-min detour from Kappabashi.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Iyoshi+Cola+Asakusa+Rokku&query_place_id=ChIJCdYEmyOPGGARIBZriyhh-Bo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.792583,35.712497,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ American Diner Andra (Ueno)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Ueno: the viral cheeseburger dunked in a skillet of cheese. 11:30–2 lunch, 10 min from Kappabashi. Only if you skipped the market snacks.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=American+Diner+Andra+(Ueno)&query_place_id=ChIJG4Z_vJmOGGARjUQ6EKP7nu0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.781398,35.713633,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Bongen Coffee Ginza</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Ginza: Japanese-style espresso bar, 30-min line, 10–5.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bongen+Coffee+Ginza&query_place_id=ChIJP2BtW-CLGGAR_-5-Dk9pFoE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.770804,35.671071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Glitch Coffee Ginza</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Ginza: single-origin, 9–6. Coffee nerds&#x27; pick; Bongen for the vibe.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Glitch+Coffee+Ginza&query_place_id=ChIJE0xjRfqLGGARkLg8IUjcu2o'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.768632,35.668917,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Ginza Hachigou (6-seat ramen, Bib Gourmand)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Ginza: 6-seat Bib Gourmand ramen with truffle ravioli, reservation only, closed Mon (so not today).<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ginza+Hachigou+(6-seat+ramen,+Bib+Gourmand)&query_place_id=ChIJX05jZOaLGGAR2rUy9EXaYLk'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.770150,35.670548,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Iroriya Higashiginza (irori izakaya)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Higashi-Ginza: basement irori izakaya, ikura bowl, drums when the caviar comes. Dinner alt if T doesn&#x27;t come through.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Iroriya+Higashiginza+(irori+izakaya)&query_place_id=ChIJSeu70OCLGGARoLGr-u6oV_k'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.768348,35.670500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Katsudon-ya Zuicho</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Shibuya: katsudon, 8 seats, one dish. Closed Sun; a lunch alt any other day.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Katsudon-ya+Zuicho&query_place_id=ChIJCZkGEqyMGGAR72gGFgeNxEE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.695360,35.662703,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Shima (Nihonbashi steak)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Nihonbashi: the other legendary steak (Kobe sirloin, the ¥9,600 takeaway sando). Closed Sun, ~¥30k pp. Backup for T; book via byFood.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shima+(Nihonbashi+steak)&query_place_id=ChIJNb3eqeKLGGARYo0br3E36Q4'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.772896,35.679047,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Wagyumafia The Cutlet Sandwich (Nakameguro)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Nakameguro: the wagyu katsu sando. Same street as T; lunch, not dinner.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Wagyumafia+The+Cutlet+Sandwich+(Nakameguro)&query_place_id=ChIJefdmkkiLGGAR0RhNwDVxI5g'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.700435,35.644085,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Bar Zoetrope</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30</b><br/>Shinjuku: 300 Japanese whiskies, 5 min from the hotel.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Zoetrope&query_place_id=ChIJA9cRNtaMGGARrZO3HTmHkXs'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.698463,35.694500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ JB&#x27;s Tokyo (burgers, Yoyogi)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1</b><br/>Yoyogi: the best cheap cheeseburger in Tokyo, 11 seats, 5 min from Shinjuku Station. If you get back early and hungry.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=JB&#x27;s+Tokyo+(burgers,+Yoyogi)&query_place_id=ChIJI42jra-NGGARz8-Vdy1WPx4'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.702182,35.682799,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Little Nap Coffee Stand (Yoyogi Park)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1</b><br/>Yoyogi Park: cortado by the train tracks. Morning-of coffee if you&#x27;re up early.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Little+Nap+Coffee+Stand+(Yoyogi+Park)&query_place_id=ChIJUyaS0ErzGGAR6_mFuqndQ9o'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.690593,35.672094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>02 Kanazawa · while you're here</name>
<Placemark><name>☆ Hakuichi (gold-leaf ice cream)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2</b><br/>Higashi Chaya: the gold-leaf soft serve, ¥900. Do it once.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hakuichi+(gold-leaf+ice+cream)&query_place_id=ChIJ12QUl3Qz-F8Rf8aIc9cRDwc'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.666475,36.572314,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Amano Tea Shop (Higashi Chaya)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2</b><br/>Higashi Chaya: tea shop with a tatami room in back; matcha set with a sweet, ~¥1,300.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Amano+Tea+Shop+(Higashi+Chaya)&query_place_id=ChIJD_dkRHMz-F8RNv6ifBwLKEY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.665815,36.573196,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Kanazawa Castle Park</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2</b><br/>Next to Kenroku-en: the rebuilt white castle, free grounds, 20 min if you want it. (teamLab&#x27;s castle show was a 2023 one-off; nothing scheduled for Dec 2026.)<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kanazawa+Castle+Park&query_place_id=ChIJlUfxPYIz-F8RSh7ml54YJ6g'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.658845,36.565946,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Turban Curry (Kanazawa curry)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2</b><br/>Hirosaka: Kanazawa&#x27;s thick black curry with a katsu, ¥1,200, 5 min from Kenroku-en. Lunch alt if the market line is long.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Turban+Curry+(Kanazawa+curry)&query_place_id=ChIJw2HKQYAz-F8RxAPmgKWGxxI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.655181,36.561889,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>03 Kyoto · while you're here</name>
<Placemark><name>☆ Gyukatsu Katsugyu Sanjo-Kawaramachi</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4</b><br/>Across the street from the hotel, B1: gyukatsu (rare beef cutlet you finish on a stone), 4.9 across 4,300 reviews, 10:30am–10:30pm. The any-day lunch.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gyukatsu+Katsugyu+Sanjo-Kawaramachi&query_place_id=ChIJU5Oa7OMJAWARwF_Lbib3xrs'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.768630,35.008654,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Hikiniku to Come (Gion)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4</b><br/>Gion: hamburg steak course grilled over charcoal in front of you, refillable rice. Reserve; closed Wed. Lunch or dinner alt any day but Dec 9.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hikiniku+to+Come+(Gion)&query_place_id=ChIJY28nVm4JAWARwfSwGp7gxk0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.774575,35.005097,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Pontocho Alley</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4</b><br/>Out the back door: the lantern lane along the river. Walk it tonight on the way home.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pontocho+Alley&query_place_id=ChIJP2DblBgJAWARAgLlF0vWT6o'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.771044,35.003934,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Tenryu-ji</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5</b><br/>Arashiyama: the Zen garden, 30 min, if the rickshaw leaves you time before lunch.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tenryu-ji&query_place_id=ChIJk54PuAGqAWARwEgz_9o-nM0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.673765,35.015838,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Arashiyama Bamboo Grove</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5</b><br/>Arashiyama: the grove on foot, 20 min, if you want it without the rickshaw.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arashiyama+Bamboo+Grove&query_place_id=ChIJrYtcv-urAWAR3XzWvXv8n_s'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.671301,35.016819,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Gion Komori (warabi mochi)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7</b><br/>Gion: warabi mochi on tatami, 11–6:30, cash. Closed Tue, so today, not tomorrow.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gion+Komori+(warabi+mochi)&query_place_id=ChIJDSr9RuoIAWARsw05VvoRb5w'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.774607,35.005842,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Itoh Dining by Nobu (Gion)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7</b><br/>Gion: Nobu&#x27;s Kyoto room, wagyu + black cod miso. Dinner backup if Mouriya&#x27;s room is gone.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Itoh+Dining+by+Nobu+(Gion)&query_place_id=ChIJxbCtcOoIAWARfuiDAOw-zJk'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.774160,35.005139,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>04 Osaka · while you're here</name>
<Placemark><name>☆ Takoyaki Wanaka Dotonbori</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9</b><br/>Dotonbori: the takoyaki line locals stand in. Let them cool 5 min.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Takoyaki+Wanaka+Dotonbori&query_place_id=ChIJza-i6hHnAGAR07AQeEhDkh0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.502730,34.668774,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Chibo Dotonbori (okonomiyaki)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9</b><br/>Dotonbori: the okonomiyaki institution, griddled at your counter. If you&#x27;d rather sit than stand before Kokuryu, skip the tray.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chibo+Dotonbori+(okonomiyaki)&query_place_id=ChIJk9v34BTnAGAR8SL3pWF-3Js'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.503838,34.668855,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Rikuro&#x27;s Namba (jiggly cheesecake)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9</b><br/>Namba: the jiggly cheesecake, baked in front of you, ¥1,000. Grab one on the walk home; breakfast tomorrow.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rikuro&#x27;s+Namba+(jiggly+cheesecake)&query_place_id=ChIJK2A0qGznAGARxPHcddHFYYA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.501566,34.666127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Bear Paw Cafe (Uehonmachi)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10</b><br/>Uehonmachi: a bear&#x27;s paw hands you your parfait through a hole in the wall. Cute, slow, 15 min from the hotel.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bear+Paw+Cafe+(Uehonmachi)&query_place_id=ChIJiWw4hHvnAGARtMh6YnrFVOQ'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.518642,34.666578,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ The Spa at Four Seasons Osaka</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10</b><br/>Dojima: the Four Seasons spa, 10 min from Umeda. A massage + ofuro soak instead of the second mall hour, if Mom wants it. Book ahead.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Spa+at+Four+Seasons+Osaka&query_place_id=ChIJVQHAl5vnAGAR0P0kuLzg1Mo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.493593,34.696121,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Mr. Hiro Car Studio (JDM garage + cafe)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10</b><br/>Taisho: a JDM dream garage with a café and simulators, 5.0 across 3,700 reviews. Dad&#x27;s, if he&#x27;s a car guy; 25 min from Namba.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mr.+Hiro+Car+Studio+(JDM+garage+++cafe)&query_place_id=ChIJI5z19PTnAGARqCxr7S7_H0g'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.471870,34.656676,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Universal Studios Japan</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10</b><br/>If you&#x27;d trade the whole Umeda/Yamazaki day: Super Nintendo World + Harry Potter. It&#x27;s a full day and a 10,000-step crowd. Not worth it for two 50-year-olds who don&#x27;t game; left here so you can overrule.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Universal+Studios+Japan&query_place_id=ChIJXeLVg9DgAGARqlIyMCX-BTY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.432319,34.665677,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Katsuo-ji (daruma temple, Minoh)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10</b><br/>Minoh: the temple of 10,000 red daruma dolls, 1 hr out by train + bus; pair with Minoh Falls (40-min walk down). The better trade for the Umeda afternoon if you want nature over malls.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Katsuo-ji+(daruma+temple,+Minoh)&query_place_id=ChIJtX8053n5AGARND16wXHGXg0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.491087,34.865775,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>05 Seoul · while you're here</name>
<Placemark><name>☆ Myshopper (personal color)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 12</b><br/>Sinsa: the 16-type personal color analysis, 1 hr, ~$100. Squeeze in before Park Jun if Reberry runs short.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Myshopper+(personal+color)&query_place_id=ChIJr9RmQmajfDURfz0pyNU27u4'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.032398,37.523121,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Seongsu-dong (alt afternoon)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 12</b><br/>Seongsu-dong: the Brooklyn of Seoul. Already on tonight&#x27;s route.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Seongsu-dong+(alt+afternoon)&query_place_id=ChIJgQD8o5OkfDUR6b0_C5FwjNk'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.056632,37.540685,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>06 Tokyo, last night · while you're here</name>
<Placemark><name>☆ Tokyo Tower</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13</b><br/>Shibakoen: walk under it after dinner, lit till 11. You don&#x27;t need to go up.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tokyo+Tower&query_place_id=ChIJCewJkL2LGGAR3Qmk0vCTGkg'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.745433,35.658580,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Yakiniku Coco Nemaru Ginza</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13</b><br/>Ginza: wagyu yakiniku in private rooms, 1 min from Ginza Stn. The swap if two sushi counters is one too many.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yakiniku+Coco+Nemaru+Ginza'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.761231,35.671706,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Yoroniku Ebisu</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13</b><br/>Ebisu: the wagyu yakiniku omakase. Book a month out. Other swap.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yoroniku+Ebisu'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.711806,35.646357,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Shima (Nihonbashi steak)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13</b><br/>Nihonbashi: closed Sundays, so not tonight.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shima+(Nihonbashi+steak)&query_place_id=ChIJNb3eqeKLGGARYo0br3E36Q4'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.772896,35.679047,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Mimasu (1910 family sushi, Yotsuya)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13</b><br/>Yotsuya: 1910 family sushi, ¥4,500 omakase. Closed Sundays; a cheap lunch any other day.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mimasu+(1910+family+sushi,+Yotsuya)&query_place_id=ChIJ9YBS2-uMGGARht93gmUhZxY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.714993,35.687811,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Sushi Punch (Azabujuban)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13</b><br/>Azabujuban: omakase 7F, closed Sun. Backup for Sushi Yuu on a different night.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sushi+Punch+(Azabujuban)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.735753,35.653655,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ BUTTER Biei pancakes (Marunouchi Bldg B1)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 14</b><br/>Same building, B1: the Biei butter pancakes with a 100 g block of butter churned in the window. The other breakfast.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=BUTTER+Biei+pancakes+(Marunouchi+Bldg+B1)&query_place_id=ChIJ0TUQMf-LGGARGckAvNCVZZ8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.763639,35.680719,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Tsukiji Outer Market</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 14</b><br/>One last market breakfast instead, 15 min away, if you&#x27;d rather eat standing up.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tsukiji+Outer+Market&query_place_id=ChIJW2cLzSGLGGARXAKXv6EkbqI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.770252,35.664770,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>☆ Yaguchi Book Store (Jimbocho)</name><styleUrl>#pick</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 14</b><br/>Jimbocho: the 3-generation film-and-art bookstore, 10:30 open, 10 min from the hotel. If there&#x27;s an hour.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yaguchi+Book+Store+(Jimbocho)&query_place_id=ChIJ1T0T-hOMGGAROQIyW12-Mgs'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.757023,35.695753,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Bench · Tokyo</name>
<Placemark><name>Good Wood Terrace (jerk chicken)</name><styleUrl>#bench</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Caribbean jerk chicken in Shibuya (viral after Kanye). Novelty pick.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Good+Wood+Terrace+(jerk+chicken)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.693500,35.657800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>II II II Coffee (Akasaka, weekdays)</name><styleUrl>#bench</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Akasaka: 1-person espresso stand, weekdays 7:30–3:30. Coffee pilgrimage only.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=II+II+II+Coffee+(Akasaka,+weekdays)&query_place_id=ChIJVbJCxmeLGGARVoHoBbTmUDQ'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.739394,35.667794,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Common (Roppongi cafe)</name><styleUrl>#bench</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Roppongi: big bright all-day café, matcha latte, breakfast plates.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Common+(Roppongi+cafe)&query_place_id=ChIJ1drE4CyLGGAR9-g-0v5WNCI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.733337,35.664112,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Onibus Coffee Yakumo</name><styleUrl>#bench</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Yakumo: the roaster&#x27;s flagship, banana bread with espresso butter. Out of the way.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Onibus+Coffee+Yakumo&query_place_id=ChIJCaW9Ty31GGARd3cEq5taDM0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.671069,35.625949,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Bench · Kyoto</name>
<Placemark><name>Marufukuro (Tadao Ando, ex-Nintendo HQ)</name><styleUrl>#bench</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Birthday-nights hotel option, Dec 7–9. Tadao Ando inside Nintendo&#x27;s 1889 HQ. ~$500–700/night.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marufukuro+(Tadao+Ando,+ex-Nintendo+HQ)&query_place_id=ChIJaaNt6YIJAWARL2yVsTV42nw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.766270,34.991777,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
